28. Subsequent events
Long-term debt
In February 2025, the Company repaid, at maturity, the remaining balance of U.S. $642 million ($930 million) on its 2.90% 10-year Notes.
In February 2025, the Company also entered into a U.S. $500 million ($715 million) unsecured non-revolving term credit facility (the "term facility") with a due date of August 6, 2025. The agreement requires the Company to maintain a financial covenant in conjunction with the term facility.
Share repurchase program
On February 27, 2025, the Company announced that the TSX has accepted its notice of intention to implement a normal course issuer bid, commencing March 3, 2025, to purchase up to approximately 37.35 million Common Shares for cancellation on or before March 2, 2026.
